  "summary": "Fix an intermittent failure in the functional test `p2p_orphan_handling.py` during peer disconnection. The test now waits for `getorphantxs()` to reflect peer cleanup before bumping mock time, ensuring orphan state and in-flight requests are removed before asserting new parent requests.",
  "problem": "In `p2p_orphan_handling.py`, disconnecting a peer does not instantly invoke `TxDownloadManager::DisconnectedPeer` if the message handling thread still holds a reference to the disconnected `CNode`. Previously, the test only waited on the connection count and a ping before advancing mock time, which could cause a split `getdata` request and fail the assertion on peer parent requests.",
